13 boxes and 38821 states in total, with complete raw stdout and actual byte
comparison. Record input capsules, context copies and hashes, Python flags,
site/cache choices, full child commands including each `ldd`, loader configs,
observed modules/mappings and before/after runtime hashes. No sample replaces
any original state. A failed assertion is preserved and reported; literal
or cutoff repair requires a separate disposition, not overwriting evidence.

Source nonhits are not clearance. The primary flip-sort paper is directly
available and its actual relevant body is read; it owns the ordinary
all-run reversal primitive and inversion potential. HXC source checking
remains bounded discovery, not a global novelty claim. These maps are author
scouts only and cannot be independently reviewed by their contributor.
