## Proof outcomes and deduction boundary

**ORR** reverses odd-length maximal increasing runs of a permutation.
`PRECODE_PROOFS.md` proves its fixed locus, convergence via a nonsharp
inversion potential, parity preservation and exact nonredundant interval
inverse. `ORR_FIBRE_PROOF.md` adds the complete all-parameter maximum:
$|T^{-1}(y)|\le F_n$ for $n\ge1$, attained uniquely at the decreasing target
when $n\ge3$ (boundary cases explicit). The proof injects inverse partitions
into odd compositions by coding an even block $r$ as $(r-1,1)$, and proves
injectivity by a target-dependent parser. It is not inferred from a table.
Ordinary interval/composition counting and inversion growth are deducted.
The tempting global height $\lfloor(n-1)/2\rfloor$ fits the original
$n\le7$ boxes, but is not proved; no causal-interval/frozen-interior lemma
was established. There is no qualifying nontrivial temporal-plus-independent
inverse contract and no gate request.

**HXC** replaces each edge by XOR with its least other intersecting edge,
holding isolated edges and merging duplicate outputs. `PRECODE_PROOFS.md`
proves that the full recurrent locus consists exactly of disjoint-edge
families; a mutual least-neighbour pair forces strict cardinality loss.
`HXC_AND_DESK_BOUNDARIES.md` gives nested families attaining the generic
$|H|-1$ bound for arbitrary edge count on a varying ground set. This is a
symbolic construction, not a larger pilot, and not the sharp clock at fixed
ground-set size. No structural full-target inverse or general fibre extremum
is proved. The actual complete target census cannot supply that missing axis.

The same boundary document supplies the explicit old CS update/centralizer
adapter for the rejected triangular-matrix desk. This is not another
executed candidate or a claimed new class. Both pilot maps remain closed
negative/partial author evidence, not paper contracts.

